# T-1066 Step 3: is_builtin_opaque — builtin type constructors (Seq, Map) stay as
# TypeApplication leaves after expand_named. They have builtin_type = Some("Seq") /
# Some("Map"), so expand_named returns TypeApplication(TypeConstructor(name), args)
# without structural expansion.
#
# `f` is annotated `@Seq` — a bare Seq annotation. The annotation resolver calls
# expand_named("Seq", [], ...) which detects is_builtin_opaque = true and returns
# TypeApplication(TypeConstructor("Seq"), []) — no structural expansion of Seq.
#
# A user-defined type alias that has Seq as its body (references a builtin-opaque TyCon)
# also takes the is_builtin_opaque path when expand_all_tycon_apps encounters Seq.
# This is a regression test: S-859 must not break Seq annotation handling.
#
# At runtime: `f` takes any sequence and returns its head element.
# `result` is the first of [1 2 3]. No === warn section asserts zero type warnings.
[
  f: [fn [let xs@Seq] [head xs]]
  result: [f [each [1 2 3]]]
]
=== out
Dict({"f": Function(xs), "result": Int(1)})
